// Package orm holds the errors that repositories generated by kanna-orm and their scopes return, and the Clock they use
// for the creation and update times of rows. Code you write by hand uses these subpackages:
//
//   - [github.com/go-kanna/orm/scope]: Of, the one field of a scope type you declare.
//   - [github.com/go-kanna/orm/option]: the options a repository's constructor takes.
//   - [github.com/go-kanna/orm/hook]: the functions that those options take and that run around each statement.
//   - [github.com/go-kanna/orm/pgx]: DBTX, the interface repositories use to run on pgx.
//   - [github.com/go-kanna/orm/stdlib]: DBTX, the interface repositories use to run on database/sql.
//
// [github.com/go-kanna/orm/change] holds Set, which the Of method of a generated change set returns. Hand-written code
// does not name it. [github.com/go-kanna/orm/impl] holds what the generated code runs on, and only generated code
// imports it.
package orm
